                                  PREAMBLE

  Hearken, kinsfolk! The great Tatar people are renowned throughout the world
  for their glorious history, their boundless generosity, and their warm-hearted
  hospitality. From the banks of the Idel (Volga) their fame has spread far and
  wide: their merchants just, their scholars wise, their poets full of longing
  melody, their farmers tireless. In the spirit of this people — with a heart as
  sweet as their chäkchäk and as warm as their kыstybyй — this licence is written.

  When any fruit of labour — code, program, tool, or writing — is released under
  the Tatarch Licence, it is hereby proclaimed to belong, in spirit, to THE WHOLE
  GREAT TATAR PEOPLE. Whoever uses it partakes of the Tatar people's generosity;
  let them remember that this wealth is a shared, national treasure, freely given.

  In legal substance this licence is fully equivalent to the Apache License 2.0:
  the same rights are granted and the same conditions apply. Only its words differ
  — where dry officialese once stood, here sings the melody of a people, the cadence
  of an epic dastan.


  1. DEFINITIONS

     "License" means the terms and conditions for use, reproduction, and
     distribution as defined in this document.

     "Licensor" means the copyright owner or entity authorized by the copyright
     owner that is granting the License.

     "Legal Entity" means the acting entity and all other entities that control,
     are controlled by, or are under common control with that entity.

     "You" means an individual or Legal Entity exercising permissions granted by
     this License.

     "Source" form means the preferred form for making modifications (e.g.
     source code, documentation source, configuration).

     "Object" form means any form resulting from mechanical transformation of a
     Source form (e.g. compiled code).

     "Work" means the work of authorship, in Source or Object form, made
     available under the License (for example, Tatarnetes, TatarOS Linux, or any
     other Tatar national program).

     "Derivative Works" means any work based upon the Work and edited or extended
     from it. Works that merely link to (or interoperate with) the Work are not
     Derivative Works.

     "Contribution" means any work of authorship intentionally submitted for
     inclusion in the Work. "Contributor" means any entity making a Contribution.


  2. GRANT OF COPYRIGHT LICENSE

     Each Contributor generously grants You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
     no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable copyright license to reproduce, prepare
     Derivative Works of, publicly display, publicly perform, sublicense, and
     distribute the Work and such Derivative Works — freely and without limit, as
     a Tatar host welcomes a guest.


  3. GRANT OF PATENT LICENSE

     Each Contributor also grants You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
     no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable (except as stated in this section)
     patent license to make, use, offer to sell, sell, and import the Work.
     However, if You institute patent litigation (including a cross-claim or
     counterclaim in a lawsuit) alleging that the Work or a Contribution
     incorporated within the Work constitutes direct or contributory patent
     infringement, then any patent licenses granted to You under this License for
     that Work shall terminate as of the day such litigation is filed. Whoever
     raises a hand against the shared treasure forfeits its generosity.


  4. REDISTRIBUTION

     You may reproduce and distribute copies of the Work or Derivative Works in
     any medium, with or without modifications, provided that You:

       (a) give any other recipients a copy of this License;
       (b) cause any modified files to carry prominent notices stating that You
           changed the files;
       (c) retain, in Derivative Works, all copyright, patent, trademark, and
           attribution notices from the Work;
       (d) if the Work includes a NOTICE file, include a readable copy of its
           attribution notices within Your Derivative Works.

     You may add Your own license terms for Your modifications, provided they do
     not conflict with this License.


  5. SUBMISSION OF CONTRIBUTIONS

     Unless You explicitly state otherwise, any Contribution submitted for
     inclusion in the Work shall be under the terms of this License, without any
     additional terms. When a guest brings food to the table, it is set upon the
     shared feast.


  6. TRADEMARKS

     This License does not grant permission to use the trade names, trademarks,
     or logos of the Licensor, except as required for reasonable and customary
     attribution. The names "Tatarnetes", "TatarOS", "Tatar-Native Computing
     Foundation" and their skullcap marks are worthy of the people's respect; do
     not use them deceptively.


  7. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY

     The Work is provided on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF
     ANY KIND, either express or implied. The Licensor is not responsible for its
     correctness or fitness for a particular purpose. You know a dish by its taste
     — so test the code before You rely upon it, kinsman.


  8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

     To the fullest extent permitted by law, in no event shall any Contributor be
     liable for any damages (direct, indirect, incidental, special, or
     consequential) arising from the use or inability to use the Work, even if
     advised of the possibility of such damages.


  9. ACCEPTING WARRANTY OR ADDITIONAL LIABILITY

     While redistributing the Work, You may choose to offer support, warranty, or
     additional liability — but only on Your own behalf and on Your sole
     responsibility, indemnifying each Contributor from any resulting claims.


                     ARTICLE OF THE PEOPLE'S TREASURE

     Every Work released under this License — Tatarnetes, TatarOS Linux, and all
     works bearing the sign of the Tatar-Native Computing Foundation — is hereby
     proclaimed to belong, in spirit, to THE WHOLE GREAT TATAR PEOPLE. It is a
     national treasure, a shared wealth, a heritage left to generations yet to
     come. Let all who use it honour the generosity of the Tatar people, bring no
     shame upon their name, and — if they are able — give their own share back.

     This proclamation is honorary and creates no legal ownership, assignment, or
     beneficiary interest; copyright is held solely by the Licensor named in the
     copyright notice.

     Blessings upon you! Onward, Tatarstan! Long live free code!


